11) Unregister / stop / check task results
-----------------------------------------
If you need to stop the scheduled job, remove it, or inspect why it failed, use the commands below.

- Stop a currently running scheduled task immediately:

    schtasks /End /TN "Obsybox_GetSystemStats"

- Delete the scheduled task (remove from Task Scheduler):

    schtasks /Delete /TN "Obsybox_GetSystemStats" /F

  Or in PowerShell (unregister):

    Unregister-ScheduledTask -TaskName "Obsybox_GetSystemStats" -Confirm:$false

- Check task registration, Last Run Time and Last Run Result (human readable):

    schtasks /Query /TN "Obsybox_GetSystemStats" /V /FO LIST

  Or with PowerShell objects:

    Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "Obsybox_GetSystemStats" | Get-ScheduledTaskInfo

- Inspect Task Scheduler operational log for errors (Event Viewer):

    # Show recent Task Scheduler events for the task
    Get-WinEvent -LogName 'Microsoft-Windows-TaskScheduler/Operational' | Where-Object { $_.Message -like '*Obsybox_GetSystemStats*' } | Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, LevelDisplayName, Message -Last 50

- Check the wrapper log produced by `run_get_system_stats.cmd`:

    Get-Content C:\Logs\obsybox\get_system_stats.log -Tail 200

Notes:
- "Last Run Result" is an exit code returned by the task process; 0 usually means success. If you see non-zero codes, check the wrapper log to see Python exceptions or stderr output.
- If you created the task under a specific user, you may need to run the unregister command as that user or as an Administrator.
- If you see permission denied or network access errors, consider running the task under an account with the required privileges instead of SYSTEM.

12) Undeploy helper (local)
---------------------------
We added an undeploy helper script that stops and removes the scheduled task, removes the wrapper, and (optionally) deletes the log file.

Run as Administrator from the repo root (example):

    .\systemMonitoring\ComputeMonitoring\undeploy_task.ps1

To also delete the log file:

    .\systemMonitoring\ComputeMonitoring\undeploy_task.ps1 -RemoveLog

Equivalent raw commands (if you prefer):

    schtasks /End /TN "Obsybox_GetSystemStats"
    schtasks /Delete /TN "Obsybox_GetSystemStats" /F

And remove wrapper/log files manually, if needed:

    del "C:\Users\Admin\Documents\Arduino\obsybox\systemMonitoring\ComputeMonitoring\run_get_system_stats.cmd"
    del "C:\Logs\obsybox\get_system_stats.log"

Notes: the helper is idempotent and safe to run multiple times; if the Task Scheduler UI still lists the task after running the helper, delete it in the Task Scheduler GUI.

